  "title": "India-US Trade Tensions Revisited and New Risks",
  "summary": "India-US trade and investment ties have been under strain for over a year, with new risks of up to 100% tariffs for continuing to buy Russian oil, as highlighted by USTR Greer's statements. Marco Rubio is set to visit India in the coming weeks.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "India faces 100% tariffs on oil and gas from Russia as US President Trump waives sanctions and tariffs under the Graham Law.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "India's Russian oil imports have been at close to current levels after the Trump waiver, with analysts noting that the law allows for up to 100% tariffs on major buyers of Russian crude.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The waiver does not provide lasting certainty, as Washington can restore tariffs anytime, leaving India and other buyers uncertain about future US action.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
